CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Verifies [expr.new] and [expr.delete]: non-array new runs the
constructor and returns a valid pointer; delete runs the destructor
exactly once.  Array new with a braced-init-list initializes each
element; array delete runs at least one destructor.
